From 29ee06eb82a31703b1e7594a7f3a0a457baa7ec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:48:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(serve): a restarted backend serves the previous
 process's kanban annotation instead of waiting cold [daveey]

After 4739e83caee (boot prewarm) the 2 h soak on hermes-hub (t_01a18b5c8b3db19c) still had 2811 AnyIO worker
samples blocked at _annotation_snapshot's cold lock wait, all in the ~20 s after each of the three
hermes-always-on-dashboard restarts (07:12, 07:52, 08:39Z): the Desktop reconnects ~3 s after start, so the
prewarm read (~1.2 s uncontended) ran 15-17 s under the burst and up to 11 /api/profiles/sessions polls waited
5-6 s.

The stale-while-refresh snapshot lived only in memory, so every restart started cold. kanban_annotation_disk now
writes the last published annotation to <HERMES_HOME>/cache/kanban-annotation/<scope-hash>.json (when it changes,
or at half its max age), and a cold poll that finds a read under way serves a same-scope copy at most 300 s old.
Rows served from the copy are stamped kanban_observed_at = the copy's time, never now; the process's own first
read replaces it. Off under HERMES_TEST_ISOLATION (tests set FORCE) so tests sharing a scope cannot leak a copy.
_mark_kanban_unknown moves to kanban_activity_identity.mark_unknown to keep the module under its line cap.
